    "Chapter-wide pattern: וְאֶת־מִגְרָשֶׁיהָ is rendered *with its suburbs*, so the waw takes *with* under rule 14, the object marker is unrepresented under rule 16, and noun and suffix split under rule 18. The competing reading marks the waw unrepresented and calls *with* added; rule 14 forbids that, since the ASV does render the connective, just not as *and*.",
